{"ts": "2026-11-21T23:46:50.661556Z", "run_id": "r-20261121T2346Z-af9e", "unit": "openspec:add-tool-adapters", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-002", "target": "C-f287b385", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The frozen test of the base unit runs the exact scenario: it grants G_LOOKUP, deploys, starts live run r_1, calls authorize for LOOKUP on the live invoker and asserts the V1 permit, isIssuedPermit true, one decision row with action invoke_tool, principal User tenant_a/alice, resource Block tenant_a/read-then-pay/lookup, node lookup, allow, one reason, that permit, 0 gateway calls and 0 effect_intent rows. The production authorize still records the decision through recordDecisionOwnTx before answering and answers the decision's permit for a fixture binding. The verifier ignored the test only because it predates this unit and has no red record, and the proposal states that rows R1 to R15 and C1 to C10 stay unchanged.", "text_sha256": "4f3190e6230f0729996b53ffa23af8fca1ebab3e395ca1f52d620d844b5390c7", "answer_sha256": "714eb3f2be0890e55fb8ccddde9495f2dfd83813bf73eda32556b48684b5f444", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-21T23:46:50.662872Z", "run_id": "r-20261121T2346Z-af9e", "unit": "openspec:add-tool-adapters", "seq": 6, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-003", "target": "C-8b5cbc41", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The frozen test runs rows E1 to E5 and E7 on one harness whose policy wrapper takes the check answer from the row: E1 to E3 throw policy_error with decisionId and errorCount and leave deny rows with their errors and no permit, E4 and E5 throw policy_unavailable with code ECONNREFUSED and UNKNOWN and add no row, E7 answers once and then throws decision_unrecorded leaving the first row; it asserts 0 gateway calls, 0 intents and that no error text contains POLICY_SET_UNAVAILABLE, PDP_EVALUATION_ERROR or db down. The production code throws those reasons with those details.", "text_sha256": "f4f0a5a2007dc8c39372db05c9ed302638c9deb756dd184ae0ab0949494b596b", "answer_sha256": "74555db9eda4f08624631f109b0eeee207c6847ebd26a65d5a7ff68fce4a0164", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-21T23:46:50.663817Z", "run_id": "r-20261121T2346Z-af9e", "unit": "openspec:add-tool-adapters", "seq": 7, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "C-c28f570f", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The four frozen tests cover rows R1 to R15: the rig test checks each refusal reason and details in order with node and no decisionId, the hook row adding hook pay:post:notify, and asserts check and connect counts 1 only for R9 and gateway 0 in every row; the R11 test asserts INTERPRETER_TOOL_FAILED with stage authorize and no db down text for each rejecting dependency; R12 and R15 on the harness check the initiator is reloaded per authorize, the version and catalogue once, and that a rejected or null approver is not loaded. The production authorize implements this order, with the new adapter_unavailable step inserted after surface_drift as the modified requirement states and checked by this unit's own tests.", "text_sha256": "5b47daa08c64dc74d2cec7c578a232c601c926a2c5c0c840beb01e9b924db161", "answer_sha256": "71192c4011f654e9b826fcc213d904b042e89fd033b4e65c6f8baf2df0290dd3", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-21T23:46:50.664765Z", "run_id": "r-20261121T2346Z-af9e", "unit": "openspec:add-tool-adapters", "seq": 8, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-005", "target": "C-17a3e8b7", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The seven frozen tests cover rows C1 to C10: C1 asserts the output, one issued token with serviceId S, agent ursitoare-engine and TTL 60 and one fake tools call with callHeader r_1:lookup:1, host, path and body digest D_LV; C2 and C3 assert upstream with status and that logs hold neither brokerServiceToken nor injected_failure; C4 to C6 assert the redirect is not followed and non-JSON bodies fail not_json with one request each at the local upstream; C7 and C8 use their own harness and assert token and send stages; C9 asserts unauthorized twice with no new token and C10 asserts one answer then unauthorized with one token and one send. The production invoke consumes the authorization on entry, rebuilds the request, requests one token, sends, and maps each failure as the requirement states.", "text_sha256": "5d05d5bcdd267a6d94707ac8411fe4318eb9640a03cd8809eb905daa4040686b", "answer_sha256": "a703aaba09d63f73c540c45c0e79192691c39c4105d3f6b00afbb53291ed5f37", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
